WEBVTT

00:38:59.410 --> 00:39:02.126
AG: That experience taught Scott
a powerful lesson.

00:39:02.150 --> 00:39:06.646
SK: Oh absolutely. I mean,
I always realize things could be worse.

00:39:06.670 --> 00:39:08.694
AG: This brings us to a third destination

00:39:08.718 --> 00:39:12.031
to transport yourself
to alternative time lines,

00:39:12.055 --> 00:39:14.726
things that could have
happened but didn't.

00:39:14.750 --> 00:39:16.789
It's called "counterfactual thinking."

00:39:17.742 --> 00:39:20.874
Psychologists have shown
that imagining how things could be worse

00:39:20.898 --> 00:39:22.984
helps us find gratitude.

00:39:23.008 --> 00:39:24.508
There's evidence, for example,

00:39:24.532 --> 00:39:27.246
that people who graduate from college
during a recession

00:39:27.270 --> 00:39:29.110
end up being happier with their jobs

00:39:29.134 --> 00:39:30.787
a decade later.